class CashDispenser {
    // largest denomination first
    private final TreeMap<Integer,Integer> inventory = new TreeMap<>(Comparator.reverseOrder());

    // returns the bills to hand out, or empty if the amount can't be made
    Optional<Map<Integer,Integer>> dispense(int amount) {
        Map<Integer,Integer> plan = new LinkedHashMap<>();
        int remaining = amount;
        for (var e : inventory.entrySet()) {
            int note = e.getKey(), available = e.getValue();
            int need = Math.min(remaining / note, available);  // greedy take
            if (need > 0) { plan.put(note, need); remaining -= need * note; }
        }
        if (remaining != 0) return Optional.empty();            // cannot make exact amount
        plan.forEach((note, cnt) -> inventory.merge(note, -cnt, Integer::sum)); // commit
        return Optional.of(plan);
    }
}
```
*This is a fast candidate builder, not a complete combination search. Use it only with a validated note policy or add a bounded-search fallback before committing inventory.*

```java
record AttemptPolicy(int maxFailures) {}

class AuthSession {
    private int failures;
    int recordFailure() { return ++failures; }
    void clearFailures() { failures = 0; }
}

class AuthService {
    private final BankGateway bank;
    private final AttemptPolicy policy;

    AuthService(BankGateway bank, AttemptPolicy policy) {
        this.bank = bank;
        this.policy = policy;
    }

    boolean verify(AuthSession session, Card card, char[] pin) {
        try {
            boolean ok = bank.verifyPin(card.token(), pin);
            if (ok) session.clearFailures();
            else if (session.recordFailure() >= policy.maxFailures()) {
                bank.blockFurtherAttempts(card.token());
                AuditLog.record("AUTH_BLOCKED", card.maskedNumber());
            }
            return ok;
        } finally {
            Arrays.fill(pin, '\0'); // best effort for the local mutable buffer
        }
    }
}
```
*The sample avoids persistent PIN storage and full card identifiers. A real ATM follows issuer and payment-network security controls.*

